<VI _name="lvdqmh_place_frame_handler.vi" description="Puts a handler subVI into one message frame of a DQMH Main.vi and wires it by NAME - the step Delacor leaves to a person with a #CodeNeeded label. The frame is found by its Case selector name among every Case Structure on the block diagram, nested ones included. Inside the frame the first node of each requested class is taken as the argument source (the Unbundle By Name of the message arguments), the error source (Variant To Data) and the reply sink (the Bundle By Name of the reply payload). With Dry Run TRUE nothing is changed and the answer lists what was found, so a caller can check the names first. Otherwise the handler is created with New VI Object, Arg Names are wired from the argument source to the handler, Error Pairs from the error source to the handler, Reply Pairs from the handler to the reply sink, every free text in the frame matching Delete Text Pattern (a regular expression, e.g. ^#CodeNeeded) is deleted; an empty pattern deletes nothing, and Main.vi is saved in place.\0A\0AMain.vi is reached in the ACTIVE PROJECT's application instance\3A a scripting edit made in any other instance reports success and changes nothing. Requires lvbd_connect_by_names.vi, generated from the AIXML beside this one, to be open when this VI is generated.">
